  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere and solid cylinder of identical radii approach an incline with the same linear velocity (see figure). Both roll without slipping all throughout. The two climb maximum heights <math><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></math> on the inline. The ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi></math> is given by:<br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0185_0d096752f2f5.png\" />"
  },
